DECISIONS 429, CODEGEN.md §3.5: a cpp emit whose mode check refused still shares its namespace with the names every mode's plan declares, so two packages writing `record X` into sov::gen collide (E8005), the refused one included.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// X.
record X {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "sov::gen", mode: zzmode }
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// X.
record X {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/b", namespace: "sov::gen", mode: baked }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8009]  a/a.canon:9:61
  invalid mode zzmode for emit cpp: expected one of baked, embedded, data, types

error[E8005]  b/b.canon:9:6
  cpp: X is generated for both a.X and b.X; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
